[Music]  what's up guys thanks for joining us  again here at the playstation  competition center for more videos on  soul calibur 6.  rip and markman here once again this  time we're going to be going over the  basics of attacking blocking and moving  now attacking is more than just matching  buttons on a controller it's important  to know how each attack works in  conjunction with each other to become a  better player  let's see how they work there are three  different attack buttons in soul calibur  6  horizontal attacks vertical attacks and  kicks  the game will use the shorthand of a b  and k to talk about these since it's  describing the moves a lot easier  there's also a guard button called g to  block attacks and soul calibur you must  hold the guard bite  holding back on the controller does not  work for the most part attacks and soul  calibur can hit at three different  heights  we call these high mid and low  in order to defend against high and mid  attacks hold the guard button while  standing  to block lows you must hold down your  controller along with guard  importantly if you are crouch blocking  mid attacks will hit you  but high attacks will always miss over  your head ah but to fully understand how  attacks are built in soul calibur you  must also understand something called  the eight way run  soul calibur is especially famous for  its fast fluid movement and eight way  run exemplifies this  simply hold any direction on the  controller to move in that direction  including diagonally  or double tap a direction to move more  quickly you can weave  in and out of your opponent's attacks  and even access special attacks that are  only available  while running in certain directions this  is important because movement is crucial  for defense  vertical attacks are often strong  offensive tools that hit mid but they  are almost always dodged by simply  moving up or down  horizontal attacks meanwhile are great  at hitting people trying to move and  they're often some of your fastest  attacks  but many horizontals are high attacks so  you can just crouch onto them  and then to hit someone who is crouching  you should use a mid-hitting vertical  attack again  this forms an interesting mind game that  is pretty unique to soul calibur  since movement is so effortless and  crucial to your strategy  if you're running into some difficult  attacks think about how moving out of  the way might help you handle it  is also useful of course but it has some  drawbacks if you block too many attacks  your health bar will start to flash  yellow  and then red eventually guarding a  powerful attack on a red health bar will  shatter your guard completely  leaving you wide open for a huge attack  if you press l1 on your controller  you'll perform a powerful vertical  attack  called the brake attack this attack is  especially good at damaging your  opponent's guard if it's blocked  but because the l1 brake attack is a  vertical attack you can sidestep it and  avoid blocking it entirely  using horizontal attacks to catch  players that are moving around or using  vertical attacks to catch players that  are scared to move is a core aspect of  fundamental  soul calibur 6 gameplay right and  instead of just button mashing you know  try to react to what your opponents are  doing  are they crouching a lot are they using  eight-way run a lot maybe they're using  horizontal attack or vertical attack  paying attention to this and reacting  accordingly will help you a lot more in  the long term  that'll do it for this episode this  tutorial was made in partnership with  the playstation competition center team  you can sign up for their open series  competitions on compete.playstation.com  subscribe to the bne esports channel for  more tutorials and soul calibur 6  content

